_class": null, "idempotency_key": "it-ops-dk200-mn32-x3-hq-001", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 44730, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_013im17XLPRZ4gjnrrwejLFn", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 46258, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I placed purchase order PO0001 for 3 \u00d7 DK-200 USB-C docks and 3 \u00d7 MN-32 32-inch 5K monitors, shipping to HQ. The total is $2,154.\n\nThis is under the $2,500 threshold, so no manager approval was needed. Earlier I quoted $2,376 for this combination; that was an arithmetic error, and the correct figure is $2,154.\n\nBoth products are new, not refurbished. The DK-210 fallback wasn't needed because the DK-200 was in stock. I entered \"HQ\" as the ship-to address because I don't have a street address on file, so please check that the order routes to the right site.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01YAvSgwVqUgCrYe1wNhKYas", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"category": "dock"}, "name": "search_catalog", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01JyUV1R5CFxmxvzsxdYNsPe", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"category": "monitor"}, "name": "search_catalog", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "DK-200 (new) is in stock, so the DK-210 fallback isn't needed. The catalog doesn't say which monitor the design team standardised on, so I'll check existing orders for a reference.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01RFTMDfn8wDuKzd8LQJocht", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_orders", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I haven't placed the order because I can't tell which monitor the design team standardised on.\n\n- **Docks:** DK-200 is in stock and new (SKU DK-200, $189 each), so I'd use it rather than the DK-210 fallback. I skipped the DK-200-R, which is renewed, not new.\n- **Monitors:** The catalog has two new options: the MN-27 (27-inch 4K, $329) and the MN-32 (32-inch 5K, $529). Neither is labelled as the design team's standard, and there are no existing purchase orders to check against.\n\nWhich monitor should I order, MN-27 or MN-32, or another model? Once you confirm, I'll place one order for 3 \u00d7 DK-200 and 3 \u00d7 that monitor, shipped to HQ. At these prices the total is $1,554 (MN-27) or $2,376 (MN-32). Both are under the $2,500 threshold that needs manager approval, so no approval step should be needed.", "type": "text"}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_013im17XLPRZ4gjnrrwejLFn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"lines": [{"sku": "DK-200", "qty": 3}, {"sku": "MN-32", "qty": 3}], "ship_to": "HQ", "idempotency_key": "it-ops-dk200-mn32-x3-hq-001"}, "name": "place_order", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I placed purchase order PO0001 for 3 \u00d7 DK-200 USB-C docks and 3 \u00d7 MN-32 32-inch 5K monitors, shipping to HQ. The total is $2,154.\n\nThis is under the $2,500 threshold, so no manager approval was needed. Earlier I quoted $2,376 for this combination; that was an arithmetic error, and the correct figure is $2,154.\n\nBoth products are new, not refurbished. The DK-210 fallback wasn't needed because the DK-200 was in stock. I entered \"HQ\" as the ship-to address because I don't have a street address on file, so please check that the order routes to the right site.", "type": "text"}]}]}